{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBRmUG2C59CkZ5BCHsrb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 8 (Pb 0.52 / Sb 0.48)** as the best composition. Its EQE was about 0.0084%, the highest of the three I measured, but it's still very low in absolute terms.\n\n| Index | Pb / Sb | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0.72 / 0.28 | −0.0023 |\n| 8 | 0.52 / 0.48 | 0.0084 |\n| 12 | 0.37 / 0.63 | 0.00075 |\n\n- **Choosing where to measure:** I spent four of the five XRD scans first (indices 2, 8, 15, 23) to map phases along the line. Index 8 matches a phase I read as the 1:1 lead antimonate Pb₂Sb₂O₇, which should absorb at the 2.7 eV illumination. From index 15 onward, a peak at Q ≈ 1.18 Å⁻¹ appears that I attributed to PbSb₂O₆, which likely has a band gap too wide to absorb there. Both phase assignments are my own peak matching and are not confirmed.\n- **Result:** EQE was highest near the 1:1 composition and fell off on both sides.\n- **Main uncertainty:** With only three EQE measurements I couldn't check the neighbours of index 8 (roughly indices 5–7 and 9–11). The best composition in the library could be one of those. I also didn't measure anything more Sb-rich than index 12, so ruling out that end rests on the phase reading and the downward trend from 8 to 12.\n\nOne XRD scan was left unused."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":9321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"547c412f-7dea-408e-b33e-582a43ad61e8","uuid":"4a883b0f-8bf2-4758-9d66-6c6910ae792f","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:06:14.879Z","request_id":"req_011CfBRmTkFzsd6ZY8o2ScLt"}
